WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.310
Grain by grain, Tibetan monks lay coloured
sand into a huge and detailed pattern.

2
00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:09.110
It can take days, or even weeks.

3
00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:12.850
Then, when it is finished,
they sweep it all away.

4
00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:16.150
Why would monks spend weeks
making a picture out of sand,

5
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.000
and then sweep it away?

6
00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:21.450
In this mission, you'll hear
the best-known Tibetan mantra,

7
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:24.830
and the quality it is meant
to grow in all who chant it.

8
00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:28.630
Then you'll meet the diamond vehicle,
the Tibetan path of Buddhism,

9
00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:30.800
and its four main schools.

10
00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:36.050
Your mission: find out why such careful
work is made only to be swept away.
